==Ukrainian==

===Etymology===
Created in {{der|uk|orv|-}} following {{m|orv|азъбукы}}, borrowed from {{der|uk|cu|азъбоукꙑ}}, formed from the names of the first two letters in the [[Cyrillic alphabet]], {{m|cu|азъ}} + {{m|cu|боукꙑ}}, a {{calque|uk|grc|ἀλφάβητος|nocap=1}}.

Attested 1627, compare {{m|uk||язъбука}} (17–18th century).

===Pronunciation===
* {{uk-IPA|а́збука}}
* {{audio|uk|Uk-азбука.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{uk-noun|а́збука|f-in|а́збуки|а́збуки}}

# {{lb|uk|dated}} {{l|en|alphabet}} {{gloss|an ordered set of letters used in a language}}, especially the old [[Cyrillic]] alphabet.
#: {{syn|uk|алфаві́т|альфабе́т|абе́тка|абе́тло|q4=dialectal}}

